  <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
       7. A DIFFERENT WAY OF UNDERSTANDING — Register 3 (pale blue-grey)
       Reframe question leads. Tightened prose. Moved from position 5.
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->
  <section class="bg-[#D8DDE8] sg-r3">
    <div class="container mx-auto px-6 py-24 md:py-32 max-w-5xl">

      <!-- Section anchor: reframe question, large and prominent -->
      <div class="max-w-3xl mb-16 md:mb-20">
        <p class="font-heading text-3xl md:text-4xl lg:text-5xl text-[#0F1422] leading-tight mb-5">
          The question is not always "what is wrong with him?"
        </p>
        <p class="font-heading text-2xl md:text-3xl lg:text-4xl text-[#A87C35] leading-snug">
          Sometimes the better question is: "What has he not yet been given?"
        </p>
      </div>

      <h2 class="font-heading text-2xl md:text-3xl text-[#0F1422] leading-tight">
        A Different Way Of Understanding The Problem
      </h2>
      <span class="h2-accent"></span>

      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4 font-body text-base text-[#1A1F2E]/80 leading-relaxed mb-14">
        <p>For most of human history, the transition into adulthood did not happen in isolation.</p>
        <p>Young men were gradually shaped through responsibility, challenge, guidance, brotherhood, mentorship, embodied practice, meaningful expectations, and relationships with older men capable of helping them mature psychologically and emotionally.</p>
        <p>Today, many young men are attempting to navigate that transition largely alone.</p>
        <p>They are surrounded by stimulation, information, pressure, comparison, distraction, and performance demands, yet often lack meaningful spaces where they can slow down enough to develop genuine self-understanding, emotional steadiness, direction, and internal structure.</p>
        <p>In many cases, the issue is not simply motivation.</p>
        <p>It is disconnection:<br class="hidden sm:block" />
        from self,<br class="hidden sm:block" />
        from responsibility,<br class="hidden sm:block" />
        from embodied presence,<br class="hidden sm:block" />
        from meaningful challenge,<br class="hidden sm:block" />
        and from trustworthy forms of guidance.</p>
      </div>

      <!-- What This Work Is, and What It Is Not: three blocks -->
      <div class="border border-[#1A1F2E]/12 rounded-2xl p-8 md:p-10 bg-[#1A1F2E]/5 mb-12">
        <h3 class="font-heading text-xs text-[#A87C35] mb-8 tracking-widest uppercase">
          What This Work Is, and What It Is Not
        </h3>
        <div class="grid md:grid-cols-3 gap-6 md:gap-8">
          <div>
            <p class="font-heading text-sm text-[#0F1422] mb-3">Not Performance Coaching</p>
            <p class="font-body text-sm text-[#1A1F2E]/72 leading-relaxed">
              This work is not focused on turning young men into hyper-productive achievement machines or forcing them into externally imposed identities. The goal is grounded self-awareness, responsibility, resilience, and inner stability.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-heading text-sm text-[#0F1422] mb-3">Not Passive Emotional Processing</p>
            <p class="font-body text-sm text-[#1A1F2E]/72 leading-relaxed">
              While emotional reflection is important, this work is not based on endless analysis without movement or accountability. Insight must gradually become embodied through action, responsibility, communication, self-observation, and lived change.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div>
            <p class="font-heading text-sm text-[#0F1422] mb-3">Not Spiritual Escapism</p>
            <p class="font-body text-sm text-[#1A1F2E]/72 leading-relaxed">
              Meditation and breathwork are approached practically as tools for attention, nervous system regulation, and self-observation. This work is grounded in real life: relationships, study, work, discipline, health, responsibility, and honest engagement with reality.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="max-w-2xl space-y-4 font-body text-base text-[#1A1F2E]/75 leading-relaxed">
        <p>Many young men do not need to become somebody else entirely.</p>
        <p>They need support in becoming more deeply connected to themselves:
          <span class="block pl-4 border-l border-[#1A1F2E]/12 mt-2 space-y-1 text-[#1A1F2E]/62">
            more honest,<br />more grounded,<br />more capable of responsibility,<br />more emotionally mature,<br />and more able to consciously shape the direction of their lives.
          </span>
        </p>
        <p>That process rarely happens through advice alone. It happens slowly through relationship, reflection, challenge, practice, and trust built over time.</p>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

